// The built-in functions and methods (`builtin` and `method` nodes).
//
// Wherever the host language has the same operation it is used directly:
// this interpreter runs on the real thing, so `s.to_upper()` is the host's
// `to_upper` and an `IoError` is the host's, renamed into the program's own
// prelude type. What is written out here is what the reference interpreter
// decides for itself -- the higher-order methods, which call back into the
// program, and every panic message the reference words in its own way.
import eval
import load
import value

/// The largest string or buffer the reference will build (`MAX_ALLOC`).
let MAX_ALLOC = 8589934592

